+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The user plays and sees links congesting but has no data on WHAT is actually
+happening — flows, hashing/routing, QoS bugs are invisible. Arch §7.2/§7.4/§7.6 specify
+the capture layer (the deterministic per-tick event stream `state.events` + the flow's SLA
+counters + the drop sites) but nothing EXPORTS it; §7.6's debug overlay was never
+scheduled.
+
+**Approach:** Add a deterministic per-tick stats record DERIVED from the existing state
+(the flow SLA accumulators, the bundle view, the per-tick drop sites, the T1 sim hash —
+no new capture semantics, no wall-clock, no render sampling), serialized as a CSV stream
+written by BOTH the harness and the app via `--stats-out <path>` (format choice: CSV —
+rationale in the PR body), plus a compile-gated debug overlay (`D` key,
+`-define:PP_DEBUG=true`) showing per-pipe readout, per-class table, congestion heat, a
+global line and a live event tail.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- **Derivation-only telemetry.** Every emitted number is a pure function of the existing
+  serialized/deterministic state (topology, bundles, flow SLA counters, per-tick drop
+  sites, health meter, `state_hash`). Zero new sim-state fields, zero new capture
+  semantics, zero RNG draws, zero clock/file reads in the derivation. Replay must
+  reproduce the exact stream (the pin).
+- **CSV stream, byte-deterministic.** Same seed + same commands → identical bytes.
+  Integer formatting only (no floats — ODN-10). Row order fixed (G row, then C rows in
+  class order, then P rows in pipe-slot order, then D rows in drop-site order). All core
+  derivation lives in `core/stats.odin` (pure; whitelisted `core:*` imports only) so the
+  harness and the app share ONE serializer.
+- **Overlay compile-gated.** `when #config(PP_DEBUG, false)` (verified: `-define:PP_DEBUG=true`
+  flips it). Release + harness builds carry ZERO overlay code. The overlay is OFF by
+  default, toggled by `D` (free: R/T/E/S/B/1/2/U/X/DEL/P/SPACE/ESC/ENTER are taken).
+  It draws ONLY from the app's HUD pass (never `draw_world`), and the harness capture
+  path never builds with PP_DEBUG — T1/T2 cannot shift by construction.
+- **The harness keeps captures clean** (documented in the PR body): harness builds never
+  pass `-define:PP_DEBUG`, so the overlay file is compile-excluded; the overlay is also
+  app-loop-only. Both layers guarantee AC4.
+- **Golden discipline:** zero catalog edits, zero demo edits, zero serializer edits —
+  NO golden re-bless. Full `harness run` must stay byte-green before + after.
+- **ASCII-only render strings** (lint gate 6 scans app/render + app/main literals).
+- **Per-sim-tick emission.** The harness's pause (5.3) is a wall-clock artifact; the
+  stream records one row set per STEPPED sim tick (drop sites are per-tick-cleared in
+  `flow_step`, so reading them right after the step is honest). Replay steps the same sim
+  ticks (pause schedule is run setup) → identical streams.
+
+**Ask First:** (none — briefing pins + ACs are the contract; any conflict HALTs)
+
+**Never:** no gameplay/balance/command changes; no new command kinds; no LOG_VERSION bump;
+no changes to `serialize.odin` / `state_hash`; no wall-clock or `core:time` in core; no
+new demos/goldens; no catalog edits; no overlay pixels in the harness capture path; no
+Perkins-visible golden shift.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| `harness run <demo> --stats-out <path>` | single demo + flag | writes the CSV stream (header + per-stepped-tick G/C/P/D rows); two runs byte-identical | flag with ≠1 demo → usage error; unwritable path → logged failure (never silent) |
+| `app --stats-out <path>` | flag on launch | app writes the same stream format per stepped tick; written at window close | unwritable path → eprintln + exit 1 |
+| paused demo (5.3) | pause schedule in the demo | stats rows exist only for stepped sim ticks (paused wall ticks emit none) — live == replay | — |
+| no traffic yet (boot.dem) | idle run, no pipes/packets | G rows every tick; C/P/D rows absent-when-empty (golden-stability rule) | — |
+| pipe in a 2-member bundle | parallel pipes (bundle.dem) | each member pipe row carries the BUNDLE's load columns (pooled link) + its own lane weights/caps | dead pipe → no row |
+| `D` key (PP_DEBUG build) | app running | overlay toggles on/off; all five elements render with real numbers | non-PP_DEBUG build → D does nothing (code absent) |
+| overlay + golden capture | PP_DEBUG build running `harness run` | overlay NEVER in captures (harness never defines PP_DEBUG; overlay is app-loop-only) | — |
+| unknown flag position | `--stats-out` in the demo list | parsed out before demo-name resolution | missing path token → usage error |
+
