+## Design Notes
+
+- **Why CSV (not JSONL):** the stream's contract is byte-determinism + diffability — the
+  user wants to SEE and DIFF the artifact. Integer-only rows in fixed order make CSV
+  trivially byte-identical (no float formatting, no quoting/escaping edge cases), diffable
+  with plain tools, and grep-able per tick. JSONL buys structure the debug loop doesn't
+  need and risks formatting drift (the JSON-int-to-float trap class — the project already
+  deleted JSON for state for exactly this reason). CSV it is; the header carries the
+  column legend as `#` comment lines.
+- **Row kinds** (one line each, tick-tagged so each line is self-contained):
+  - `G <tick>,<gen>,<sim_hash_hex>,<score>,<meter_pct>` — global line.
+  - `C <tick>,<class>,<demand>,<delivered>,<dropped>,<loss_pct>,<avg_latency_ms>,<sla_lat>,<sla_loss>`
+    — per class with demand (absent-when-empty); SLA math identical to `sla_evaluate`
+    (integer division, monotone loss).
+  - `P <tick>,<pipe>,<tier>,<cap_units>,<offered>,<carried>,<dropped>,<util_pct>,<we>,<ws>,<wb>,<ce>,<cs>,<cb>,<qe>,<qs>,<qb>`
+    — per live pipe. Load columns (cap/offered/carried/dropped/util/queues) are the pipe's
+    BUNDLE (the pooled link — the honest capacity unit); lane columns are the pipe's own
+    weights (w) + the flow's derived lane caps (c) + the bundle's per-lane queue depths (q).
+  - `D <tick>,<pipe>,<class>,<reason>,<count>` — this tick's drop sites, per (pipe, class,
+    reason) — the "dropped by class + Drop_Reason" breakdown.
+- **Metric definitions (documented in the PR body):** `carried` = queued packets ×
+  packet_bandwidth (the in-flight load on the link); `offered` = carried + this tick's
+  drops × bandwidth (demand presented vs shed — offered ≥ carried, the gap is the drops);
+  `util_pct` = min(100, carried × 100 / bundle_cap) — the congestion-heat number. All
+  derived, all integer.
+- **The sim hash** rides the G row (the harness already computes it per tick — pass it in;
+  the app computes `state_hash` per step, pure + cheap at 20 Hz).
+- **Replay-identity by construction:** the stream is a pure function of state + the
+  per-tick drop sites, and the pause schedule is run setup — so live and replay emit the
+  same rows for the same sim ticks. The `stats-check` verb pins it through the REAL
+  replay path (blessed log + manifest), not a duplicate loop.
+- **Overlay data = stream data:** the overlay reads the same `stats_compute` record
+  (per frame in the app; the stream writes the same record per step) — the numbers the
+  user sees under `D` are the numbers the stream pins. One derivation, two consumers.
+- **Event tail:** read-only tail scan of `state.events` (the app never drains — the 4.2
+  tripwire; the overlay READS the last 8, never drains, never filters forward).
+
