+# Story 5.7 — Runtime telemetry (stats stream + debug overlay)
+
+Implements arch §7.2/§7.4/§7.6 (the scheduled telemetry): a deterministic per-tick
+stats stream (`--stats-out <path>`, CSV) written by BOTH the harness and the app,
+plus a compile-gated debug overlay (`D` key, `-define:PP_DEBUG=true`).
+
+## What this is
+
+- **`core/stats.odin`** — the per-tick `Stats_Record`, derived ONLY from existing
+  deterministic state (the flow SLA accumulators, the bundle view, the per-tick
+  drop sites, the health meter, the T1 sim hash). Zero new capture semantics, zero
+  wall-clock, zero RNG. `stats_write_csv` is the ONE serializer both binaries share
+  — byte-identity by construction.
+- **Harness** — `harness run <demo> --stats-out <path>` writes the stream through
+  the real run loop; `harness stats-check <demo>` pins REPLAY-IDENTITY (live stream
+  == replay-from-blessed-log, byte-for-byte, through the real replay path).
+- **App** — `app --stats-out <path>` writes the same stream per stepped tick;
+  `D` toggles the debug overlay (per-pipe readout, per-class table, congestion
+  heat, global line, live event tail).
+- **`harness overlay-check <demo> <ms>`** (PP_DEBUG builds only) renders the SHIPPED
+  overlay over a demo frame to a PNG — the AC3 verification vehicle.
+
+## The stream (CSV — why not JSONL)
+
+The contract is byte-determinism + diffability; the user wants to SEE and DIFF the
+artifact. CSV with integer-only rows in fixed order is trivially byte-identical (no
+float formatting, no quoting/escaping edges) and diffable/grep-able with plain
+tools. JSONL's structure buys nothing the debug loop needs and risks formatting
+drift — the project already deleted JSON-for-state for exactly that trap class.
+
+Row kinds (header carries the legend as `#` lines):
+- `G <tick>,<gen>,<sim_hash_hex>,<score>,<meter_pct>`
+- `C <tick>,<class>,<demand>,<delivered>,<dropped>,<loss_pct>,<avg_latency_ms>,<sla_lat>,<sla_loss>`
+- `P <tick>,<pipe>,<tier>,<cap_units>,<offered>,<carried>,<dropped>,<util_pct>,<wE>,<wS>,<wB>,<cE>,<cS>,<cB>,<qE>,<qS>,<qB>`
+- `D <tick>,<pipe>,<class>,<reason>,<count>` — this tick's E9 drops by class+reason
+
+**Metric definitions** (all derived, all integer): `carried` = queued packets ×
+packet_bandwidth (the in-flight load on the link at the step boundary); `offered` =
+carried + this tick's drops × bandwidth (demand presented vs shed — the gap is the
+loss); `util_pct` = min(100, carried × 100 / bundle_cap) — the congestion heat. Load
+columns are the pipe's BUNDLE (the pooled link is the honest capacity unit, 2.1);
+lane columns are the pipe's own dial + the flow's derived per-pipe caps.
+
+**Emission rule:** one record per STEPPED sim tick (a 5.3 paused wall tick is
+stable, and the drop sites are per-step scratch — a paused record would be a lie).
+The pause schedule is run setup, so live and replay step the same sim ticks →
+identical streams (pinned by `stats-check`).
+
+## Sample stream — `qos_contention` (the ~2.4x oversubscribed pipe, tick 21)
+
+Verbatim from `harness run qos_contention --stats-out` (a fresh run at this sha):
+
+```
+G,21,11,3065d3ada10b1ef9,3,100
+C,21,0,12,1,5,83,250,0,1
+C,21,1,12,2,2,50,375,1,1
+P,21,0,1,15,270,240,1,100,1,1,1,5,5,5,2,0,6
+P,21,1,1,15,180,180,0,100,1,1,1,5,5,5,0,6,0
+P,21,2,1,15,0,0,0,0,1,1,1,5,5,5,0,0,0
+P,21,3,1,15,0,0,0,0,1,1,1,5,5,5,0,0,0
+D,21,0,0,0,1
+```
+
+Pipe 0 (cap 15) is offered 270 units, carrying 240, util 100% (the congested link);
+pipe 1 (the return leg) offered 180/cap 15, util 100%. The one D row this tick:
+pipe 0 shed an email packet (class 0, reason 0 = Queue_Overflow). Email loss 83%,
+streaming 50% — both SLA-breached. This is the congestion the user wanted to SEE,
+now pinned as bytes.
+
+## The overlay (`D`, PP_DEBUG builds only)
+
+The briefing's user-approved list, mapped onto the stream: per-pipe readout (on
+select), per-class table (demand/delivered/dropped/loss%/avg ms/SLA), congestion
+heat (pipes tinted by util% — ladder <50 clear / 50-69 amber / 70-89 orange / ≥90
+red), the global line (tick/gen/hash/score/meter), and the live event tail (last 8,
+human-readable, read-only tail scan — never drains, never filters forward).
+
+**Build flag:** `odin build app -define:PP_DEBUG=true` (or `odin run app
+-define:PP_DEBUG=true`). Release/plain builds compile ZERO overlay code (the whole
+file is `when #config(PP_DEBUG, false)`-gated).
+
+**Golden safety (AC4) — three layers:** (1) the overlay file is compile-excluded in
+every non-PP_DEBUG build — the harness NEVER builds with the define, so its capture
+path cannot contain a pixel of it; (2) the overlay is OFF by default (D toggles);
